  <static seed="27" source="Contrib/CCCS/AlgebraicLiteracy/IA_7.2/OpenStax_IA_7.2_121.pg">
    <statement><p>Add or subtract the rational expressions.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{{\frac{p}{p-8}} - {\frac{p-10}{p+8}} = }</m><fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{26p+\left(-80\right)}{\left(p+8\right)\mathopen{}\left(p-8\right)}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>The LCD must contain each factor from each denominator, so the LCD = <m>{\left(p+8\right)\mathopen{}\left(p-8\right)}</m>.</p>
<p>We need to rewrite each expression with the LCD:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ {\frac{p}{p-8}} \cdot \frac{p+8}{p+8} - {\frac{p-10}{p+8}} \cdot \frac{p-8}{p-8} }</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \frac{{p^{2}+8p}}{{\left(p+8\right)\mathopen{}\left(p-8\right)}} - \frac{{p^{2}-10p-8p+80}}{{\left(p+8\right)\mathopen{}\left(p-8\right)}} }</m></p>
<p>Notice the subtraction applies to every term in the 2nd fraction:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{\frac{{p^{2}+8p}}{{\left(p+8\right)\mathopen{}\left(p-8\right)}} + \frac{{-p^{2}+18p-80}}{{\left(p+8\right)\mathopen{}\left(p-8\right)}}}</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{{\frac{26p-80}{\left(p+8\right)\mathopen{}\left(p-8\right)}}}</m></p>
</solution>
